.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Minimizes a convex quadratic over the triangle \{x \geq 0,\ x_1 + x_2 + x_3 = 1\} without ever projecting onto it. Each step solves a linear program, whose solution is a vertex, and moves toward that vertex. The Frank-Wolfe gap certifies how far the objective is from optimal.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/optimization/constrained/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_02_frank_wolfe_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/optimization/constrained/plot_02_frank_wolfe`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Frank-Wolfe: optimization over the probability simplex</div>
    </div>


.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/optimization/constrained/plot_02_frank_wolfe`

.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Fiacco and McCormick&#x27;s sequential unconstrained minimization replaces \min x^2+y^2 subject to x+y=1 with the unconstrained problems \min x^2+y^2+\mu(x+y-1)^2 for growing \mu. Each penalized minimizer violates the constraint slightly, and the violation shrinks like 1/\mu as the minimizers approach the constrained optimum (0.5, 0.5).">

